brief:
The desktop app (React + TypeScript, folder desktop/) shows workflows on the 'Workflows SOP' screen through desktop/src/services/workflowApi.ts. That file still expects the OLD backend's shapes and crashes with 'users is not iterable'. Rewrite it for the NEW backend (smurf-server).

NEW backend endpoints (use the existing helpers `serverFetch` and `SERVER_BASE` imported from './serverUrl', exactly as the file does today):
- GET  /api/workflows/user  -> { workflows: Graph[] }
- GET  /api/workflows/user/<id> -> { graph: Graph }
- PUT  /api/workflows/user/<id> body { graph: Graph } -> { status: 'saved' | 'invalid', problems: string[] }
There are NO template endpoints and NO validate endpoint any more.

Graph type (add it to workflowApi.ts and export it):
  type GraphNode = { id: string; type: string; name?: string; params?: Record<string, unknown>; position?: [number, number] };
  type GraphEdge = { from: string; port?: string; to: string };
  type Graph = { id?: string; name: string; description?: string; start: string; nodes: GraphNode[]; edges: GraphEdge[] };

Required changes in workflowApi.ts:
1. Export a pure function `graphToCompiler(id: string, g: Graph): CompilerWorkflow` (CompilerWorkflow is imported from './workflowFormat' - read that file for its exact fields and follow them). Mapping: add a node {id:'start', type:'start'} with an edge to g.start; every graph node becomes a node whose type is 'human_gate' if node.type starts with 'human.', 'check' if it starts with 'verify.', otherwise 'agent_task'; its data holds { agent: node.type, instruction: node.name ?? node.type, params: node.params ?? {} }; position from node.position ([x,y] -> {x,y}). Every graph edge becomes an edge from->to; put the port name (edge.port ?? 'out') in the edge data under the key the CompilerEdge type uses for branch labels (check workflowFormat.ts) only if it is not 'out'. Use name = g.name and description = g.description.
2. fetchUserIds(): read { workflows } and return the ids (workflow.id).
3. loadUserWorkflow(id): GET /api/workflows/user/<id>, return graphToCompiler(id, body.graph).
4. fetchTemplateIds() returns [] without any request; loadTemplateWorkflow throws Error('no templates'); loadWorkflowById(id) = loadUserWorkflow(id); validateWorkflow resolves without a request.
5. saveUserWorkflow and deleteUserWorkflow: throw Error('Editing workflows from the app is not available yet; edit workflows/*.json') without a request.
6. listWorkflowItems(): one request to GET /api/workflows/user, map each graph to { id, name, source: 'user', readOnly: true, description }. Keep the exported names and signatures so other files keep compiling.

Also create desktop/src/services/workflowApi.test.ts (vitest) with at least 3 tests for graphToCompiler: start node + edge to g.start; 'human.approval' -> 'human_gate' and 'verify.evidence' -> 'check'; a port like 'retry' is kept on the edge while 'out' is not. Do not change any other file.
